{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_0135czWpkTR7s4xdqzTHvLMm", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/6821545\"}, {\"url\": \"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/5683738\"}, {\"url\": \"https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/5612080\"}, {\"url\": \"https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0375239NWB1/document.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://patents.google.com/patent/US4983413\"}, {\"url\": \"https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0184259NWB1/document.xml\"}, {\"url\": \"https://patents.google.com/patent/US5612080\"}, {\"url\": \"https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0375239NWB1/document.xml\"}, {\"url\": \"https://brevets-patents.ic.gc.ca/opic-cipo/cpd/eng/patent/1326162/summary.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://patents.google.com/patent/US4508746\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T13:06:54.243Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Mattson Volpenhein patent 3,600,186 low calorie fat-containing food compositions", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01Pxs9qTjVndcxRV92KKvtLK", "content": [{"title": "Low calorie fat materials that eliminate laxative side effect", "url": "https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/6821545"}, {"title": "Low calorie fat substitute", "url": "https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/5683738"}, {"title": "Low calorie fat substitute", "url": "https://image-ppubs.uspto.gov/dirsearch-public/print/downloadPdf/5612080"}, {"title": "data.epo.org", "url": "https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0375239NWB1/document.pdf"}, {"title": "US4983413A - Low-calorie polysiloxane oil food products - Google Patents", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/US4983413"}, {"title": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>", "url": "https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0184259NWB1/document.xml"}, {"title": "US5612080A - Low calorie fat substitute - Google Patents", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/US5612080"}, {"title": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>", "url": "https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0375239NWB1/document.xml"}, {"title": "brevets-patents.ic.gc.ca", "url": "https://brevets-patents.ic.gc.ca/opic-cipo/cpd/eng/patent/1326162/summary.html"}, {"title": "US4508746A - Low calorie edible oil substitutes - Google Patents", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/US4508746"}]}, "The search didn't return the patent's own text, but several sources describe it, and they agree on the basics.\n\n- **Core claim:** Other patents describe US 3,600,186 as covering low-calorie fat-containing foods in which roughly 10 to 100 percent of the fat is a sugar or sugar alcohol fatty acid ester with at least four ester groups. (3,600,186 to Mattson refers to low calorie fat-containing food compositions wherein from about 10 percent to about 100 percent of the fat consists of a sugar fatty acid ester having at least 4 fatty acid ester groups.)\n- **Example and drawback:** One exemplified compound is a mixed sucrose octaoleate, and because it was a liquid polyester, it produced anal leakage. (One compound exemplified in the Mattson Patent is a mixed sucrose octaoleate. Since this compound was a liquid polyester, an undesirable anal-leakage effect was noted.)\n- **Applications:** A European patent says the patent covers mayonnaise and salad dressings in which the fat is partly or fully replaced by nonabsorbable polyol polyesters. (It discloses low calorie food compositions, including mayonnaise and salad dressing products, wherein at least a portion of the fat is replaced with certain nonabsorbable, nondigestible polyol polyesters.)\n- **Authorship:** Google Patents lists it as Mattson and Volpenhein, while the European patent cites it as Mattson et al., issued August 17, 1971. (3,600,186 to Mattson and Volpenhein shows sugar fatty acid esters and sugar alcohol fatty acid esters having at least 4 fatty acid ester groups.)\n\nI did not find the full claims or the official text, so I'd check the USPTO or Google Patents record for US 3,600,186 directly before relying on these details."], "durationSeconds": 7.900776917, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_0135czWpkTR7s4xdqzTHvLMm", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
